{"term":"void","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:d87a8a4e1fee9057e3","definition":"Containing nothing; empty; not occupied or filled.","example":"Today's youth's brains are sucked void of common sense.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["vacant","unfilled","empty","empty as a pauper's purse","empty as the tomb on Easter","clean","leer","toom","unfilled","vacant","vacuumlike","vacuous","void"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/void#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:98a5d8c878dec25a10","definition":"Having no incumbent; unoccupied; said of offices etc.","example":"divers great offices that had been long void","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/void#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c5bd41710da4a0608f","definition":"Being without; destitute; devoid.","example":"Suppoſe they be in number infinit,\nYet being voyd of Martiall diſcipline,\nAll running headlong after greedie ſpoiles: […]\nTheir careleſſe ſwords ſhal lanch their fellows throats\nAnd make vs triumph in their ouerthrow.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["bereft of","destitute of","absent","awanting","bereft of","deficient of","deprived of","destitute of","devoid of","lacking","leer","poor in","robbed of","shorn of","stripped of","void of","wanting"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable, with-of","register":"not-comparable, with-of","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/void#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c7abf02a9b9fc0294e","definition":"Not producing any effect; ineffectual; vain.","example":"[My word] shall not return to me void, but it shall accomplish that which I please.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["pointless","useless","bootless","barren","futile","sterile","fruitless","gainless","idle","dry","ineffectual","inefficacious","inutile","no good","otiose","pointless","profitless","purposeless","tired","unavailing","unprofitable","unuseful","unutilizable","useless","vain","void"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/void#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:149da57c76e64a2474","definition":"Of no legal force or effect, incapable of confirmation or ratification.","example":"null and void","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/void#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bcda39f8b0b1d901f1","definition":"Containing no immaterial quality; destitute of mind or soul.","example":"And senseless words she gave, and sounding strain, / But senseless, lifeless! idol void and vain!","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/void#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c894f9c7c3a01544fd","definition":"Of a function or method, that does not return a value; being a procedure rather than a function.","example":"In particular, the roll method is void — it has no return value.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-co